  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">A net reduction in physical hydrocarbon deliveries to global markets tightens available supply relative to demand and, through direct supply–demand mechanics, raises spot prices (and conversely increased flow depresses spot prices).</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_ris</data>
