  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp rises in spot oil prices drive inflation and fiscal stress, prompting governments and central banks to deploy subsidies, price controls, strategic releases, or monetary/fiscal interventions aimed at stabilizing markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_ris</data>
