<edge source="global_energy_supply_ris::storage_inventory_volume" target="ai_compute_chip_race::policy_intervention_int" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher onshore and nearshore hydrocarbon stocks reduce the need for emergency policy measures because authorities view inventories as a buffer and are less likely to trigger releases or extraordinary controls.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_ris</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_compute_chip_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_ris::storage_inventory_volume" target="china_eu_trade_rivalry::energy_supply_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Larger onshore and nearshore hydrocarbon inventories provide a buffer that can be drawn down to cover production or transit outages, directly lowering the observed rate of supply disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_ris</data>
  <data key="d40">china_eu_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_ris::storage_inventory_volume" target="iran_proxy_escalation::trade_restrictions_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid draws in global storage inventories prompt consuming and transit states to impose export restrictions, rationing or priority allocation rules to preserve domestic supplies, increasing the overall level of trade restrictions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_ris</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_ris::storage_inventory_volume" target="russia_ukraine_war::market_uncertainty" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher onshore and nearshore hydrocarbon stocks reduce ambiguity about near-term supply availability and buffer against shocks, thereby lowering collective market uncertainty among traders and policymakers.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_ris</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_ris::tanker_charter_rate" target="global_energy_supply_ris::crude_flow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
