<edge source="ai_compute_chip_race::route_security_risk" target="china_eu_trade_rivalry::tanker_attack_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising assessed risk along key sea lanes prompts opportunistic state and non‑state actors to target lightly escorted tankers and raises the measured probability of attacks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_compute_chip_race</data>
  <data key="d40">china_eu_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_compute_chip_race::route_security_risk" target="china_eu_trade_rivalry::trade_flow_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher route security risk forces shippers to reroute, slow transit, and pay much higher insurance/premiums, directly reducing the volume of energy cargoes moved between regions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_compute_chip_race</data>
  <data key="d40">china_eu_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_compute_chip_race::route_security_risk" target="global_energy_supply_ris::crude_flow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising security risks (attacks, mines, seizures or interdictions) cause port closures, convoying, rerouting around longer corridors and temporary shut-ins, directly reducing the physical throughput of crude shipments.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_compute_chip_race</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_ris</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_compute_chip_race::route_security_risk" target="global_energy_supply_ris::oil_spot_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Elevated route risks generate an immediate supply-risk premium and anticipatory buying (and insurance surcharges), pushing up spot prices even before large physical flow reductions materialize.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_compute_chip_race</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_ris</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_compute_chip_race::route_security_risk" target="iran_proxy_escalation::security_incident_freq" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">An increased assessed risk to key routes reflects more hostile activity and weaker escorts, which directly raises opportunities and incentives for Iran-aligned proxy groups and other malign actors to attack or seize tankers, pipelines and convoys, increasing incident frequency.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_compute_chip_race</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_compute_chip_race::route_security_risk" target="russia_ukraine_war::hydrocarbon_supply_flow" id="0">
