  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Interruptions to production, refining or transport caused by China–EU trade friction directly reduce available near-term supply and push benchmark crude and refined-product prices higher.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_eu_trade_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
